#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# divide_sides

#% text
# `divide_sides(rel, c)` divides every side of the equation or inequality rel by c; `divide_sides(rel)` divides by the right side.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# An inequality is reversed for a negative c; an undecided sign gives a piecewise over c > 0 and c < 0 (over c != 0 for an equation), with rel itself otherwise.

#% item
# `divide_sides(a == b, c == d)` divides side by side. `assumptions:` facts that decide the sign of c.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
divide_sides(3*x == 21, 3)
#% output
#= x == 7

#% cell
divide_sides(a*b == 3)
#% output
#= (1/3)*a*b == 1

#% cell
divide_sides(b*x > 7, b)
#% output
#= piecewise([[x > 7/b, b > 0], [x < 7/b, b < 0]], b*x > 7)

#% cell
divide_sides(a*x^2 > b*x + c, a, assumptions: a > 0)
#% output
#= x^2 > (c + b*x)/a

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `multiply_sides`, `add_sides`, `subtract_sides`
